                description: "Zyros has no idea of his origins, but what he does remember is the poor orphanage of Morrigen District where he grew up; There were other kids he shared a dream with, that they would become high mages to eventually better the district. But death does not discriminate—Losing their friends did not hinder the remaining three’s ambitions. Instead, it only made them more determined… and a young Zyros even promised to save them if they were ever in danger. But those thoughts were just the naivety of a child whose tunnel vision was anchored to ideals rather than truth. As time passed, Zyros would be confronted with humbling experiences and the reality of how far his dream was. The cynical thoughts settled in and pricked at his mind—After all, being from a disadvantageous background made the world seem much bigger and others all the stronger. So what did that matter? Well, those thoughts took a turn for the worse one day, when they got into a run-in with the wrong people. The enemy noticed Zyros’ unique power, offering a trade: a high-paying job out of Morrigen District as a contract enforcer in exchange for his friends' lives. Despite his star-touched powers and the weight of his promises, the seeds of doubt and pessimism broke through. Thus, Zyros decided not to test it to ensure his own survival. That’s right… All he has to do is to listen to those stronger than him. This was the way the fates decided their strength, and thus, how Zyros should live his life selfishly.",
